LICENSE AMBIGUITY IN THE UPSTREAM WORK
--------------------------------------
As of the fork point, the upstream repository contained no LICENSE, COPYING, or
NOTICE file in any commit on any branch, and its published npm tarballs contain
no license file. It shipped two conflicting license declarations:

  - package.json declared:  "license": "MIT"
  - README.md reproduced the Apache License 2.0 boilerplate, under the heading
    "## License / Apache License 2.0 / Copyright 2024"

Because the governing license could not be determined with certainty, this fork
is distributed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. That choice is valid under
either reading of the upstream grant: if the upstream work is MIT-licensed, the
MIT permission to sublicense allows redistribution under Apache-2.0 with the
original notice preserved; if the upstream work is Apache-2.0-licensed, then
Apache-2.0 is required. Distributing under MIT alone would not be safe under the
second reading.

STATEMENT OF CHANGES (Apache-2.0 section 4(b))
----------------------------------------------
Files in this distribution have been modified from the upstream work. The
principal changes are:

  - The primary HomeKit service was changed from Thermostat to HeaterCooler.
  - Fan speed and fan-auto control were added, on a linked HAP Fanv2 service.
  - Vane control was added (HAP SwingMode and Slat), including the device
    write path, which did not exist upstream.
  - Setpoint handling was changed to a Fahrenheit-anchored quantization grid.
  - The TargetTemperature characteristic was removed; the two threshold
    characteristics are the setpoint controls in every mode. This supersedes
    the AUTO band-collapse fix originally submitted upstream as PR #23.
  - Dry and Fan-only switches were made opt-in via configuration, alongside new
    options for the humidity sensor and the vane Slat service.
  - Wireless-sensor temperature, humidity and battery were surfaced from the
    cloud sensor_update event, including a HAP Battery service.
  - TemperatureDisplayUnits was made settable (upstream hardwired Celsius).

See CHANGELOG.md for the full list.

LATER PORTS FROM UPSTREAM
-------------------------
Upstream has since added an Apache-2.0 LICENSE file (commit 45133b2). Two features
were ported from upstream after the fork point, under that license, and adapted
to the HeaterCooler service:

  - Zombie-stream detection and recovery (upstream commit 59879da),
    in src/kumo-api.ts.
  - Adapter reachability surfaced as No Response in HomeKit (upstream commit
    7941fe1), in src/accessory.ts, src/kumo-api.ts and src/platform.ts.

